<title>MEXICO: CYCLING-FRANCE'S LONGO BREAKS WORLD ONE-HOUR RECORD.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-FRANCE'S LONGO BREAKS WORLD ONE-HOUR RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French cyclist Jeannie Longo broke the women's world one-hour cycling record on Saturday.</p>
<p>Longo covered more than 144 laps in one hour to break the record previously held by Briton Yvonne McGregor. She was on her 145th lap when the hour bell rang.</p>
<p>An official distance for her record would be announced shortly, officials at the Mexico City track said.</p>
</text>
